> on and off the trap and collecting any arrows.  But now my inventory
> looks like:
>
> p - an arrow
> q - 2 arrows
> r - an arrow
> s - an arrow
> t - 2 arrows
> etc.
>
> How do I group these arrows up in my quiver?
>

When an arrow trap fires an arrow, it is randomly generated. That is, its
properties like enchantment, BUC-status and poisoning are determined by a
formula with a random component. Objects only stack when they are identical
in all of these properties. Obviously, there's a finite umber of
combinations so if you keep on doing this, you'll eventually get big
stacks. A better way is to #untrap the trap, which generates a bunch of
arrows with identical properties.
Theoretically, you can get more arrows from repeatedly stepping on the trap
than from disarming it, but it is tedious and you are likely to get hungry
long before you have a satisfying stack, and even more likely to eventually
be hit by an arrow that was generated poisoned and die instantly.

